From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: pd_mapper: serve tms/pdr_enabled on sm6375 modem PD

0084 added sm6375 to the PD mapper but reused sm6115's domain set, which puts
the plain mpss_root_pd_gps on the modem root PD. That domain advertises
gps/gps_service but not tms/pdr_enabled.

A measurement on a Motorola Moto G82 5G (SM6375) shows that is the gap. With
qcom_pd_mapper's get_domain_list pr_debug enabled, the modem, during its boot,
queries the service registry by service name and asks for:

	PDM: service 'tms/pdr_enabled'     offset -1 returning 0 domains (of 0)
	PDM: service 'tms/pddump_disabled' offset -1 returning 0 domains (of 0)

Both are unserved. tms/pdr_enabled is the flag by which a PD-aware peripheral
learns the AP supports PDR on its protection domain; it is declared upstream
only by the mpss_root_pd_gps_pdr variant, used by sc7180 and sc7280. This is
consistent with the modem-image string

	Diag_LSM.c:servreg_get_local_domain() returned null

which is the modem's diag failing to find its enabled PD.

Give sm6375 its own domain table, identical to sm6115's set that already works
for adsp, cdsp and gps, but with mpss_root_pd_gps_pdr in place of
mpss_root_pd_gps so the modem's tms/pdr_enabled query is answered. This is a
module, so it is tested by swapping the module and rebooting, not by flashing.

Whether serving this actually makes the modem bring up diag is the next test;
this patch is the change that makes tms/pdr_enabled resolve, which the modem
was measured to ask for and not get.
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
@@ -512,6 +512,18 @@
 	NULL,
 };
 
+/* Like sm6115, but the modem root PD advertises tms/pdr_enabled, which this
+ * SoC's modem diag looks up at boot (measured on Moto G82 5G, rhodep). */
+static const struct qcom_pdm_domain_data *sm6375_domains[] = {
+	&adsp_audio_pd,
+	&adsp_root_pd,
+	&adsp_sensor_pd,
+	&cdsp_root_pd,
+	&mpss_root_pd_gps_pdr,
+	&mpss_wlan_pd,
+	NULL,
+};
+
 static const struct qcom_pdm_domain_data *sm6350_domains[] = {
 	&adsp_audio_pd,
 	&adsp_root_pd,
@@ -615,7 +627,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm4250", .data = sm6115_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6115", .data = sm6115_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6350", .data = sm6350_domains, },
-	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6375", .data = sm6115_domains, },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6375", .data = sm6375_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7150", .data = sm7150_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7225", .data = sm6350_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7325", .data = sc7280_domains, },
